Here is a clean, comprehensive template you can copy and paste into your note-taking app (like Notion, Obsidian, or a markdown file) every time you solve a new or challenging problem.

It is designed to capture the core logic and track your progress across your three focus languages.

---

```markdown
# [Problem Name]

**Platform:** [e.g., HackerRank, LeetCode]
**Pattern/Topic:** [e.g., Two Pointers, Dynamic Programming, BFS]
**Difficulty:** [Easy / Medium / Hard]
**Date Completed:** [YYYY-MM-DD]

---

### 🧠 Core Concept

**Problem Summary (In My Own Words):**
> [Write a 1-2 sentence breakdown of what the problem is actually asking you to do. Strip away the fluff from the problem description.]

**The Approach / Intuition:**
*   [Step 1 of the logic]
*   [Step 2 of the logic]
*   [Step 3 of the logic]

**Complexity Analysis:**
*   **Time Complexity:** O(...) - [Briefly explain why]
*   **Space Complexity:** O(...) - [Briefly explain why]

---

### 💻 Implementations

**C Snippet / Key Logic:**
[Focus on pointer management or manual memory allocation used here]

**Java Snippet / Key Logic:**
[Focus on the Collections Framework classes or OOP structure used here]

**Python Snippet / Key Logic:**
[Focus on Pythonic shortcuts or built-in modules used here]

---

### ⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas

*   **Edge Cases to Remember:** 
    *   [e.g., What if the array is empty?]
    *   [e.g., What if all numbers are negative?]
*   **My Mistakes (The "Bug Tracker"):** 
    *   [e.g., Hit a Time Limit Exceeded (TLE) because I used a nested loop instead of a hash map.]
    *   [e.g., Forgot to update the pointers in my while loop, causing an infinite loop.]

---

### 🔗 Connections

*   **Similar Problems:** [List 1-2 related problems to reinforce the pattern]
*   **Helpful Resources:** [Link to any YouTube videos or articles that helped you understand the optimal solution]

```
